  "scientific_caveats": [
    "Archimedes attached-frond Breckenridge County KGS fossil has no accession or species label. Model is Archimedes sp., not claimed A.kentuckiensis. Exact dimensions and300 sampled fenestrules are artistic. Original KGS image was viewed through an attributed mirror after direct502; photograph distinguished from adjacent Greb reconstruction.",
    "Penniretepora flexistriata uses SNSB-BSPG2020XCI121/122/123 and primary species description. Main/lateral widths, angle, same-rank spacing and aperturewidth follow actual cited bounds. Whole pinnate outline,16laterals and length are artistic fragment extrapolation; no fused side branches.",
    "Constellaria florida uses OUIP24 and1905 primary comparative descriptions. Depressed stellate maculae replace erroneous planning monticule wording in a documented prefreeze clarification. Broad12mmwidth and3.5mmthickness distinguish it from narrow C.emaciata. Three branches,36 maculae and fullY silhouette are artistic.",
    "Cystodictya formosa external XCI99 and crosssection XCI23c, not C.pustulosa. Width, total relief thickness,5rows and aperturewidth remain within formosa bounds. Y outline is an explicitly bounded reconstruction, not an observed intact colony.",
    "All required maculae, all required aperture rows and all structural components have actual global exposure. Some repeated tiny apertures at intended overlaps are partially or fully occluded and individually reported; no claim that all duplicate pores are visible. Finite ray sampling and macro visibility are not independent visual approval."
  ],
  "fresh_qa_focus": [
    "Personally inspect original primary text and specimen pixels. Consult-only source images andPDF stay local, never in Git.",
    "Inspect32 distinct exact-final512px views,4 lossless sheets and3 exact macro images. Distinguish Archimedes true open helix, Penniretepora free laterals/tworows, Constellaria integrated depressions/broadbranches, Cystodictya fiverows/thicknarrowbranches.",
    "Check final Cystodictya r003 original topology and actualroot contact, not superseded r002 report. Every PASS here pins its actual final subject and source hashes.",
    "Measured actual transformed widths/thickness, source-specific hard bounds, actual triangle/base contact and dense all-component exposure are verified. Integrated feature rays additionally include their host surface. No arbitrary percentage cutoff.",
    "Original final source and GLB components are closed/outward without diagnostic weld or normal recalculation. Two real separate Blender PIDs per final subject with queued input/output proofs, not loop counters."
  ],
